@startuml E3-deployment-03-orders-market-mvc
title CryptoWeb - Deployment 03: Orders and Market Feeds (MVC)

!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Client browser" as Browser {
  artifact "Market / Trades Views" as UI
  artifact "ordersApi.js / tradeApi.js" as API
}
node "Server_3 Node.js :4000" as S3 {
  artifact "Order controller" as OrderCtrl
  artifact "Mongoose Order / Trade models" as Models
  artifact "orderExecuter.js (5-10s timer)" as Executor
  artifact "market/news service modules" as MarketSvc
}
node "Core Node.js :5000" as Core {
  artifact "internal trade controller" as CoreCtrl
  artifact "trade settlement service" as TradeService
}
database "Server_3 MongoDB\norders / trades / candles / news" as Mongo
database "Core MySQL\ntrade_fills + wallet data" as SQL
cloud "Binance live prices / REST" as Binance
cloud "News RSS / market sources" as News

Browser --> S3 : orders / market APIs
S3 --> Mongo : store pending orders and synchronized trades
S3 --> Binance : WSS market stream / HTTPS
S3 --> News : RSS / HTTP ingest
S3 --> Core : internal execution REST x-internal-key
Core --> SQL : market-price settlement
Core --> Binance : execution price REST

note bottom of S3
  The order executor and market/news
  schedulers run inside the Server_3
  Node.js process (not separate servers).
  Trigger price is not a guaranteed
  execution price.
end note

@enduml
